FAQS = [["What is FLUX.2 Max?","FLUX.2 [max] is Black Forest Labs' premium FLUX.2 image-generation and image-editing model. It emphasizes high visual fidelity, consistency across reference images, detailed prompt following and optional grounding search."],["How much does FLUX.2 Max cost per image?","On Black Forest Labs' API, the first output megapixel costs $0.07, each additional output megapixel adds $0.03, and reference-image inputs cost $0.03 per billed input megapixel. Thus a 1024×1024 text-to-image result starts at $0.07, while a 2048×2048 four-megapixel result costs $0.16 before any reference-image input."],["What is the FLUX.2 Max API endpoint?","Black Forest Labs documents POST https://api.bfl.ai/v1/flux-2-max with the x-key API key header, a prompt, and optional parameters such as width, height, seed, output_format and input_image fields. Requests are asynchronous."],["Does FLUX.2 Max support image editing?","Yes. Supply an input_image and describe the requested change. Up to eight reference images can be supplied through the BFL API, while its Playground supports up to ten."],["What is the maximum FLUX.2 Max resolution?","FLUX.2 supports output images up to 4 megapixels; 2048×2048 is a four-megapixel example. The official resolution guidance lists minimum dimensions of 64×64 pixels and dimension increments of 16 pixels."],["What is grounding search in FLUX.2 Max?","Grounding search is a capability specific to FLUX.2 [max] that can search the web when prompted to incorporate timely context into images. Generated visuals should still be fact-checked against original sources."],["Is FLUX.2 Max free or open source?","The BFL-hosted FLUX.2 [max] API is a paid service. Do not confuse it with the locally deployable FLUX.2 [dev] or [klein] releases, whose weight licensing and access are separate."],["FLUX.2 Max vs FLUX.2 Pro: which should I choose?","Choose Max for premium fidelity, difficult multi-reference editing and grounding search; choose Pro for a lower-cost production workflow. Official BFL rates start at $0.07 for Max versus $0.03 for Pro for the first output megapixel. Output quality and speed depend on task and settings."],["How does FLUX.2 Max image editing pricing work?","Editing adds reference-image input charges to output-resolution charges. For example, a 2MP output plus two one-megapixel references is $0.10 for output plus $0.06 for input, totaling $0.16 at BFL's published rates. Multiple references have special resizing rules."],["How should I prompt FLUX.2 Max for product photography?","Define the product, composition, camera angle, background, lighting and any required brand colors. When editing, identify the elements that must stay unchanged and describe the exact modification; test the generated logo and text before publishing."]]
SECTIONS = "\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-overview\" data-flux2-max-guide>\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">QUICK MODEL ANSWER</p><h2>What is FLUX.2 Max?</h2></div>\n          <p><strong>FLUX.2 [max]</strong> is Black Forest Labs' premium model for <strong>text-to-image generation</strong> and <strong>reference-guided image editing</strong>. It is positioned for high-fidelity marketing visuals, realistic product photography, character consistency and complex visual instructions. Unlike a text chatbot, its main output is an image, not a token stream.</p>\n          <p><strong>At a glance:</strong> generate up to <strong>4-megapixel images</strong>, pass as many as <strong>8 reference images through the BFL API</strong> (10 in its Playground), and use the hosted <code>/v1/flux-2-max</code> endpoint. Direct BFL API pricing starts at <strong>$0.07 for the first output megapixel</strong>. Max is also the FLUX.2 variant with <strong>grounding search</strong> for incorporating real-time information when prompted. <a href=\"https://bfl.ai/models/flux-2-max\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Black Forest Labs confirms the model's positioning</a>.</p>\n          <nav class=\"model-related-links\" aria-label=\"Jump to FLUX.2 Max model sections\">\n            <a href=\"#flux2-max-pricing\"><span>IMAGE PRICING</span><strong>Calculate cost by megapixel</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n            <a href=\"#flux2-max-api\"><span>BFL API</span><strong>Endpoint, headers and polling</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n            <a href=\"#flux2-max-comparison\"><span>MODEL CHOICE</span><strong>Max vs Pro vs Klein</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n          </nav>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-specs\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">VERIFIED SPECIFICATIONS</p><h2>FLUX.2 Max specs: resolution, inputs and capabilities.</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-capability-grid\">\n            <article><span>PROVIDER AND MODEL</span><h3>Black Forest Labs</h3><p>Official family name FLUX.2 [max]; BFL API route <code>/v1/flux-2-max</code>.</p></article>\n            <article><span>OUTPUT RESOLUTION</span><h3>Up to 4 MP</h3><p>For example, 2048×2048 pixels. The FLUX.2 resolution guide lists a 64×64 minimum, dimensions in 16-pixel steps and flexible aspect ratios.</p></article>\n            <article><span>INPUTS AND OUTPUT</span><h3>Text + reference images → image</h3><p>Enter a text prompt for generation. Add reference images and a change request to edit, combine or restyle visual content.</p></article>\n            <article><span>REFERENCE CAPACITY</span><h3>8 API / 10 Playground</h3><p>BFL documents up to eight source images through the developer API and ten through the Playground; multi-reference prompts can identify image numbers.</p></article>\n            <article><span>GROUNDING SEARCH</span><h3>Max-exclusive FLUX.2 feature</h3><p>Can search the web when prompted to inform images with timely information; this is not a guarantee of factual or textual correctness.</p></article>\n            <article><span>DEPLOYMENT</span><h3>Hosted BFL API</h3><p>Commercial hosted access; pricing and parameter support on third-party runtimes such as Cloudflare can differ from BFL's own API.</p></article>\n          </div>\n          <p><strong>What not to infer:</strong> BFL's image generator does not publish a conventional chatbot knowledge-cutoff date, context-window benchmark, or text-generation output limit for this SKU in SXF's verified catalog. For image generation, resolution, references, features and megapixel cost are the meaningful specifications.</p>\n          <p>Official references: <a href=\"https://help.bfl.ai/articles/8531149640-what-are-the-resolution-limits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">FLUX.2 resolution limits</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.bfl.ai/flux_2/flux2_image_editing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">FLUX.2 editing and reference limits</a>, and <a href=\"https://help.bfl.ai/articles/7655484417-what-flux-models-are-available\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">model-family capabilities</a>.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-pricing\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">OFFICIAL API PRICING</p><h2>FLUX.2 Max price per image: examples and billing formula.</h2></div>\n          <p><strong>The frequently quoted $0.07 price is only the first output megapixel.</strong> BFL's official rate card charges <strong>$0.07 for output MP #1</strong>, <strong>+$0.03 for each additional output MP</strong>, and <strong>+$0.03 per billed reference-image MP</strong>. A megapixel in BFL's pricing definition is 1024×1024 pixels, and output and reference sizes are rounded up to whole billable MP. Output is limited to 4 MP.</p>\n          <p><strong>Base cost formula:</strong> <code>$0.07 + $0.03 × (billed output MP − 1) + $0.03 × billed reference MP</code>. Use this for the official BFL API price; do not automatically apply it to third-party providers.</p>\n          <div class=\"model-capability-grid\">\n            <article><span>1024×1024 · TEXT TO IMAGE</span><h3>$0.07 / image</h3><p>1 output MP; no source images. The entry price shown on official listings.</p></article>\n            <article><span>2048×1024 · TEXT TO IMAGE</span><h3>$0.10 / image</h3><p>2 output MP: $0.07 for the first + $0.03 for the second.</p></article>\n            <article><span>2048×2048 · TEXT TO IMAGE</span><h3>$0.16 / image</h3><p>4 output MP: $0.07 + three additional MP at $0.03.</p></article>\n            <article><span>1024×1024 · 1 REFERENCE</span><h3>$0.10 / edit</h3><p>1 output MP ($0.07) plus one 1MP input image ($0.03).</p></article>\n            <article><span>2048×1024 · 2 REFERENCES</span><h3>$0.16 / edit</h3><p>2 output MP ($0.10) plus two 1MP references ($0.06).</p></article>\n            <article><span>HIGH-VOLUME COST</span><h3>$7 / 100 images</h3><p>Illustrative cost for 100 successful 1MP text-to-image outputs; larger images, editing references and provider-specific fees increase cost.</p></article>\n          </div>\n          <p><strong>Multi-reference billing nuance:</strong> a single reference can be processed up to 4MP at its original size. With multiple reference images, BFL says sources over 1MP are reduced to 1MP and every reference is charged as one MP. Images above 4MP are resized. These rules mean input count and output dimensions both matter when estimating image-editing cost.</p>\n          <p>Verified provider source: <a href=\"https://bfl.ai/pricing?category=flux.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Black Forest Labs FLUX.2 pricing and image-resolution billing notes</a>. These are published API equivalents, not a promotional price or a guarantee of provider-specific reseller rates.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-workflows\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">GENERATE VS EDIT</p><h2>How to use FLUX.2 Max for image generation and editing.</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-capability-grid\">\n            <article><span>TEXT TO IMAGE</span><h3>Create an asset from a prompt</h3><p>Describe the subject, layout, material, lighting, lens and intended usage. For example, produce a realistic product hero image or key visual for a campaign without a reference photograph.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> “Studio product shot of a frosted amber skincare bottle on pale travertine, soft side lighting, 85mm lens, subtle shadows, label reading ‘SOLIS’, restrained editorial layout, 4:5 portrait composition.”</p></article>\n            <article><span>IMAGE EDITING</span><h3>Keep the identity, change the scene</h3><p>Attach the original image using <code>input_image</code> and specify what to modify while preserving important elements. The reference can define the product, character, wardrobe or architecture.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> “Use the bottle from image 1. Preserve its silhouette, cap and logo layout. Replace the background with a sunlit bathroom vanity, maintain natural contact shadows and keep the brand color #A65E45.”</p></article>\n            <article><span>MULTI-REFERENCE COMPOSITING</span><h3>Combine several visual sources</h3><p>Use one image for the subject, a second for a prop and a third for the environment, and refer to the numbered images in the prompt. This is useful for campaign consistency but adds reference-input cost.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> “Place the chair from image 1 in the room from image 2. Apply the fabric texture in image 3 while retaining the chair's shape, scale and perspective.”</p></article>\n          </div>\n          <p>BFL's <a href=\"https://docs.bfl.ai/flux_2/flux2_text_to_image\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">text-to-image documentation</a> and <a href=\"https://docs.bfl.ai/flux_2/flux2_image_editing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">image-editing guide</a> explain the two request patterns. For branding, review each generated letter, packaging claim and legal mark before publishing.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-api\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">DEVELOPER REFERENCE</p><h2>FLUX.2 Max API: endpoint, parameters and example request.</h2></div>\n          <p>Use <code>POST https://api.bfl.ai/v1/flux-2-max</code> with your private BFL API key in the <code>x-key</code> header. The JSON body includes a required <code>prompt</code>, optional image dimensions such as <code>width</code> and <code>height</code>, and optional image references such as <code>input_image</code> and <code>input_image_2</code>. BFL's API also documents an optional <code>seed</code>, <code>output_format</code> and <code>disable_pup</code> setting. Confirm the exact feature set in your current API reference.</p>\n          <p><strong>Minimal text-to-image cURL example:</strong></p>\n          <pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;overflow-x:auto\"><code>curl -s -X POST \"https://api.bfl.ai/v1/flux-2-max\" \\\n  -H \"accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"x-key: $BFL_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"prompt\": \"Photorealistic ceramic coffee mug on a walnut table, morning window light, shallow depth of field\",\n    \"width\": 1024,\n    \"height\": 1024,\n    \"output_format\": \"jpeg\"\n  }'</code></pre>\n          <p><strong>To edit an existing image:</strong> use the same endpoint and add <code>\"input_image\": \"https://example.com/source.jpg\"</code> to the payload, together with a prompt identifying the desired change. Additional reference fields follow the numbered pattern through <code>input_image_8</code>.</p>\n          <div class=\"model-caveat-list\">\n            <div><span>01</span><p><strong>Submit:</strong> authenticate server-side with <code>BFL_API_KEY</code>. The API returns a job identifier and a <code>polling_url</code>, not finished image bytes immediately.</p></div>\n            <div><span>02</span><p><strong>Poll:</strong> request the returned <code>polling_url</code> until <code>status</code> becomes <code>Ready</code>. Handle failed or moderated requests and apply retry limits.</p></div>\n            <div><span>03</span><p><strong>Save:</strong> retrieve the signed image URL under <code>result.sample</code> promptly; BFL says result links expire after about ten minutes.</p></div>\n            <div><span>04</span><p><strong>Secure:</strong> never expose the API key in website JavaScript or share generated output links as permanent asset storage.</p></div>\n          </div>\n          <p>Official integration references: <a href=\"https://help.bfl.ai/articles/8446125349-quickstart-guide\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BFL submit-and-poll quickstart</a> and <a href=\"https://docs.bfl.ai/flux_2/flux2_image_editing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">editing request example</a>.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-grounding\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">DISTINCTIVE FEATURE</p><h2>What is FLUX.2 Max grounding search?</h2></div>\n          <p>Black Forest Labs identifies <strong>grounding search</strong> as a Max-only FLUX.2 capability. When the prompt calls for timely context, the model can search the web and incorporate information into an image. BFL examples include weather-inspired city visualizations and topical graphics. This can be valuable when the visual should reflect current context rather than the model's static learned associations.</p>\n          <p><strong>Practical limitation:</strong> grounding is not an independent fact-checking service. If the visual displays financial data, current weather, news, public figures or numerical claims, verify the output and its labels against authoritative external sources before publishing. BFL does not claim that grounding makes every generated statement error-free.</p>\n          <p>Source: <a href=\"https://docs.bfl.ai/flux_2/flux2_text_to_image\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BFL FLUX.2 text-to-image guide: Grounding Search</a>.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-comparison\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">MODEL SELECTION</p><h2>FLUX.2 Max vs FLUX.2 Pro, Klein and Flex.</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-capability-grid\">\n            <article><span>FLUX.2 MAX</span><h3>From $0.07 · fidelity priority</h3><p>Highest-quality FLUX.2 tier according to BFL, with exclusive web grounding and strong multi-reference consistency. Choose for demanding final assets where visual quality outweighs cost.</p></article>\n            <article><span>FLUX.2 PRO</span><h3><a href=\"/models/flux-2-pro/\">From $0.03 · production scale</a></h3><p>Lower-cost professional generalist model, suitable for larger batches of product and marketing visuals. BFL lists $0.015 per additional output MP and per reference MP.</p></article>\n            <article><span>FLUX.2 KLEIN 9B</span><h3><a href=\"/models/flux-2-klein-9b/\">From $0.015 · low latency</a></h3><p>Compact, fast alternative for previews, iterative drafting and throughput-sensitive generation. Licensing differs from BFL-hosted Max.</p></article>\n            <article><span>FLUX.2 FLEX</span><h3>$0.05 first MP · typography</h3><p>BFL positions Flex for images containing text and fine-grained guidance controls. Different model settings and output tasks need direct testing.</p></article>\n          </div>\n          <p><strong>Direct price comparison at 1MP without references:</strong> Max $0.07, Pro $0.03, Klein 9B $0.015, Flex $0.05. This compares BFL's base list prices—not image-quality test results. For a different image-generation ecosystem, see <a href=\"/compare/flux-2-max-vs-nano-banana-pro/\">FLUX.2 Max vs Nano Banana Pro</a>.</p>\n          <p>Source: <a href=\"https://bfl.ai/pricing?category=flux.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">official FLUX.2 family pricing</a> and <a href=\"https://help.bfl.ai/articles/6122710168-which-flux-2-model-should-i-choose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">model-choice guide</a>.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-prompting\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">PROMPTS AND QUALITY CONTROL</p><h2>How to write effective FLUX.2 Max prompts.</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-caveat-list\">\n            <div><span>01</span><p><strong>Start with the final composition:</strong> specify subject, environment, viewing angle, crop and main visual hierarchy before adding aesthetic adjectives.</p></div>\n            <div><span>02</span><p><strong>Specify exact brand constraints:</strong> include key colors as hex values, desired materials and precisely quoted text. Then inspect letter shapes, small print and logos in the generated output.</p></div>\n            <div><span>03</span><p><strong>In editing, define both changes and invariants:</strong> tell the model what to replace and what must retain identity, scale, face, packaging or lighting.</p></div>\n            <div><span>04</span><p><strong>Use numbered references intentionally:</strong> identify which image supplies the person, product, style or location rather than asking it to infer the source of each element.</p></div>\n            <div><span>05</span><p><strong>Test at your final output size:</strong> megapixel cost grows with dimensions, and 4MP is the supported ceiling. Compare samples at the resolution you intend to publish.</p></div>\n          </div>\n          <p>These are practical production recommendations based on documented FLUX.2 prompting capabilities, not a guarantee that every prompt will produce identical or perfectly legible results.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-use-cases\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">USE CASES &amp; BOUNDARIES</p><h2>When should you use FLUX.2 Max?</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-capability-grid\">\n            <article><span>ECOMMERCE</span><h3>Consistent product photos</h3><p>Stage the same object in new backgrounds while using its original packshot as a reference. Carefully check logo and label accuracy.</p></article>\n            <article><span>CAMPAIGNS</span><h3>Hero images and key art</h3><p>Explore detailed art direction, photographic realism, material finishes and lighting for high-visibility marketing assets.</p></article>\n            <article><span>CHARACTERS</span><h3>Multi-reference identity</h3><p>Reuse consistent character and styling references across scenes, while checking the result for unexpected identity drift.</p></article>\n            <article><span>DESIGN</span><h3>Visual concepts and mockups</h3><p>Prototype layouts and typographic scenes with specified colors; validate any functional UI, factual claims and final print details separately.</p></article>\n          </div>\n          <p><strong>Trade-offs:</strong> Max is more expensive per output MP than Pro, Klein and Flex. Grounded content may still contain errors, input references increase billing, and this hosted model should not be confused with openly licensed self-hosted checkpoints. Evaluate price, speed and output quality using your own prompts.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-related\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">RELATED MODEL REFERENCES</p><h2>Continue from FLUX.2 Max to the right comparison.</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-related-links\">\n            <a href=\"/models/flux-2-pro/\"><span>CHEAPER IMAGE API</span><strong>FLUX.2 Pro specs and pricing</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n            <a href=\"/models/flux-2-klein-9b/\"><span>FAST IMAGE GENERATION</span><strong>FLUX.2 Klein 9B reference</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n            <a href=\"/compare/flux-2-max-vs-nano-banana-pro/\"><span>DIRECT COMPETITOR</span><strong>FLUX.2 Max vs Nano Banana Pro</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n            <a href=\"/providers/black-forest-labs/\"><span>PROVIDER FAMILY</span><strong>All Black Forest Labs models</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n            <a href=\"/models/pricing/\"><span>API COSTS</span><strong>SXF model pricing reference</strong><b>↗</b></a>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n"
FAQ_HTML = "\n        <section class=\"model-deep-section\" id=\"flux2-max-faq\">\n          <div class=\"model-section-head\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</p><h2>FLUX.2 Max FAQ: pricing, images, API and editing.</h2></div>\n          <div class=\"model-caveat-list\">\n            <div><span>01</span><p><strong>What is FLUX.2 Max?</strong> FLUX.2 [max] is Black Forest Labs' premium FLUX.2 image-generation and image-editing model. It emphasizes high visual fidelity, consistency across reference images, detailed prompt following and optional grounding search.</p></div>\n            <div><span>02</span><p><strong>How much does FLUX.2 Max cost per image?</strong> On Black Forest Labs' API, the first output megapixel costs $0.07, each additional output megapixel adds $0.03, and reference-image inputs cost $0.03 per billed input megapixel. Thus a 1024×1024 text-to-image result starts at $0.07, while a 2048×2048 four-megapixel result costs $0.16 before any reference-image input.</p></div>\n            <div><span>03</span><p><strong>What is the FLUX.2 Max API endpoint?</strong> Black Forest Labs documents POST https://api.bfl.ai/v1/flux-2-max with the x-key API key header, a prompt, and optional parameters such as width, height, seed, output_format and input_image fields. Requests are asynchronous.</p></div>\n            <div><span>04</span><p><strong>Does FLUX.2 Max support image editing?</strong> Yes. Supply an input_image and describe the requested change. Up to eight reference images can be supplied through the BFL API, while its Playground supports up to ten.</p></div>\n            <div><span>05</span><p><strong>What is the maximum FLUX.2 Max resolution?</strong> FLUX.2 supports output images up to 4 megapixels; 2048×2048 is a four-megapixel example. The official resolution guidance lists minimum dimensions of 64×64 pixels and dimension increments of 16 pixels.</p></div>\n            <div><span>06</span><p><strong>What is grounding search in FLUX.2 Max?</strong> Grounding search is a capability specific to FLUX.2 [max] that can search the web when prompted to incorporate timely context into images. Generated visuals should still be fact-checked against original sources.</p></div>\n            <div><span>07</span><p><strong>Is FLUX.2 Max free or open source?</strong> The BFL-hosted FLUX.2 [max] API is a paid service. Do not confuse it with the locally deployable FLUX.2 [dev] or [klein] releases, whose weight licensing and access are separate.</p></div>\n            <div><span>08</span><p><strong>FLUX.2 Max vs FLUX.2 Pro: which should I choose?</strong> Choose Max for premium fidelity, difficult multi-reference editing and grounding search; choose Pro for a lower-cost production workflow. Official BFL rates start at $0.07 for Max versus $0.03 for Pro for the first output megapixel. Output quality and speed depend on task and settings.</p></div>\n            <div><span>09</span><p><strong>How does FLUX.2 Max image editing pricing work?</strong> Editing adds reference-image input charges to output-resolution charges. For example, a 2MP output plus two one-megapixel references is $0.10 for output plus $0.06 for input, totaling $0.16 at BFL's published rates. Multiple references have special resizing rules.</p></div>\n            <div><span>10</span><p><strong>How should I prompt FLUX.2 Max for product photography?</strong> Define the product, composition, camera angle, background, lighting and any required brand colors. When editing, identify the elements that must stay unchanged and describe the exact modification; test the generated logo and text before publishing.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n"
